 spectral_norm's mixed operands)."] [234 1 "// tpName is a type's tp_name: a built-in type of another module than builtins named with it."] [242 1 "// seqConcatError is PyNumber_Add's sequence fallback when neither operand adds: str's, list's and tuple's sq_concat"] [243 1 "// and the bytes-like buffers' refuse b in their own words (nil for any other a)."] [262 1 "// overridesReflected is b's type a proper subtype of a's whose reflected method is its own."] [298 1 "// InPlaceOp is a op= b: the in-place method, else BinaryOp."] [301 17 "// int and float have no in-place methods"] [324 1 "// UnaryOp is +o, -o or ~o."] [335 1 "// RichCompare is a op b (PyObject_RichCompare: the C level's recursion check, then do_richcompare)."] [337 2 "// two exact ints or two exact floats: their own comparison, which recurses into nothing (202b)"] [357 1 "// doRichCompare is do_richcompare: b's swapped method first when b's type is a proper subtype of a's (whether or not"] [358 1 "// it overrides it), then a's method, then b's swapped one unless already tried (checked_reverse_op), then identity for"] [359 1 "// == and != (queue 264: test_binop's test_comparison_orders)."] [391 1 "// Eq is a == b as a Go bool (identity first, as PyObject_RichCompareBool)."] [403 1 "// GetAttr is getattr(o, name)."] [418 1 "// Call is f(*args) with the last len(kwnames) of args keyword arguments."] [427 1 "// GetIter is iter(o)."] [438 1 "// mappingOnly is an object whose subscription is mp_subscript alone, no sq_item for PySequence_Check: a union, a class"] [439 1 "// whose metaclass defines no __getitem__ (type's GetItem slot is the class subscription; queue 225: iter(int))."] [451 1 "// Next is next(it): (nil, nil) at the end."] [460 1 "// GetItem is o[key]."] [462 2 "// an exact list's or tuple's item at an int in range: the slot's answer without its conversions (202b)"] [493 1 "// seqIter is the iterator of a type with __getitem__ and no __iter__ (PY5b: its type registered)."] [532 1 "// isSeqRepeat is a type with sq_repeat."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[36 22] [67 22] [90 27] [97 27] [147 39] [154 36] [182 49] [193 39] [199 49] [300 39] [303 36] [313 36] [326 34] [340 23] [344 25] [363 30] [370 36] [376 36] [407 32] [429 29] [463 24] [471 28] [481 32] [484 23] [485 41] [519 29]]} (go/file "abstract.go" :imports [

